WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:02.919
Whose land is this?

00:00:04.546 --> 00:00:05.463
My land.

00:00:05.463 --> 00:00:08.591
♪

00:00:08.591 --> 00:00:09.843
William: Well, well, well.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:12.804
Our war hero has arrived.

00:00:12.804 --> 00:00:14.556
William: You made a good choice coming back here.

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:16.808
The Osage are the finest,

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:17.767
William: wealthiest,

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:19.519
William: and most beautiful people on God’s earth.

00:00:19.769 --> 00:00:21.396
William: They outsmarted everybody.

00:00:21.396 --> 00:00:22.480
♪

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.149
William: They have the say

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:25.108
William: who gets the oil.

00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:26.067
♪

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:28.069
William: Son, I got a question.

00:00:28.069 --> 00:00:28.945
You like women?

00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:30.280
That’s my weakness.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.322
[LAUGHS]

00:00:31.322 --> 00:00:33.533
♪

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.952
William: Well we mix these families together

00:00:35.952 --> 00:00:36.786
William: and that estate money

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:38.496
flows the right direction. It’ll come to us.

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:39.706
♪

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.040
Mollie: Sho-mee-kah-see.

00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:42.542
Mollie: That’s how you are.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:42.876
♪

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.169
I don’t know what you said

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:46.504
but it must’ve been Indian for handsome devil.

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:48.590
[LAUGHS]

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:53.219
♪

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.512
Why did you come here?

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:59.225
♪

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.685
Ernest: I work with my uncle.

00:01:01.352 --> 00:01:02.145
You scared of him? 

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:03.605
♪

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:04.481
No, he’s a…

00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:06.900
Ernest: the nicest man in the world.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:07.901
♪

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:08.860
William: The Osage,

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.903
William: their time is over.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.070
♪

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.615
William: We’ve got to take back control of our home.

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:15.366
♪

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:16.951
Tom: I was sent down from Washington, D.C.

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:18.411
to see about these murders. 

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.038
♪

00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:22.248
Paul: We have so many deaths we’ve lost count.

00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:23.208
William: It’s just

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:25.168
bad luck.

00:01:25.168 --> 00:01:27.962
Tom: Seems more like an epidemic than bad luck to me. 

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:30.340
♪

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.176
Paul: The Osage is dying by the enemy.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.970
Do not let them die alone. 

00:01:36.554 --> 00:01:38.848
Mollie: Evil surrounds my heart. 

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:45.814
♪

00:01:45.814 --> 00:01:46.773
William: You gotta pick a side.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.275
♪

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.569
Mollie: I don’t even know if you love me anymore. 

00:01:51.569 --> 00:01:52.779
Of course I love you.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:53.321
 ♪

00:01:53.321 --> 00:01:55.740
Mollie: Then kill these men who killed my family

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.284
♪

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.620
Tom: Did your wife say who she was most afraid of? 

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:04.082
♪

00:02:04.082 --> 00:02:06.209
[SCREAMING]

00:02:06.835 --> 00:02:08.461
William: Don’t do something you’re gonna regret

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.921
for the rest of your life. 

00:02:09.921 --> 00:02:15.718
♪

00:02:15.718 --> 00:02:17.887
Ernest: I ain’t got nothing but regret.

00:02:17.887 --> 00:02:23.893
♪

